The Moment-to-Moment Experience

1.  Engage Workload: The player triggers system cycles manually or monitors
    active daemons.
2.  Evaluate Risk Vectors: Two gauges rise concurrently:
      - Heat Gauge: Rises continuously with each cycle. Above 85°C, Thermal
        Surge activates, rapidly escalating payout multipliers while narrowing
        reaction windows.
      - RAM Allocation: Fills block-by-block. Reaching 100% RAM halts all
        generation, freezing the player in the high-heat danger zone.
3.  Execute the Flush: The player releases or hits Flush Cache. A channel time
    initiates. During this channel, the system cannot process new cycles, but
    passive cooling continues. If the flush completes before 100°C is reached,
    all unbanked Bytes safely transfer to Banked Bytes.
4.  Hardware Upgrade Cycle: Banked Bytes are spent on higher clock frequencies
    (faster throughput, more heat), liquid cooling / fans (faster heat
    dissipation), RAM sticks (larger volatile buffer), and storage buses
    (faster/higher-yield flushes).
5.  Macro Progression: Lifetime Banked Bytes level up the OS from Version 1.0 to
    Version 100.0, unlocking advanced hardware sockets, daemon slots, and Kernel
    Resets (Prestige).

