9. Idle and Automation Systems

Automation programs run as background processes ("Daemons"). They generate load,
consume continuous memory, and execute logic cycles automatically.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| DAEMON PROCESS THREAD ARCHITECTURE                                                                |
| Max Slots: 4 (Unlocked at Levels 5, 20, 40, 75)                                                   |
| System Rule: Total Daemon RAM Consumption CANNOT exceed 75% of current Max RAM                    |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

1. Auto-Process Alpha (miner_d.exe)

  - Unlocked: Level 5
  - RAM Allocation Overhead: Consumes a flat 16 MB of RAM constantly while
    active.
  - Behavior: Automatically triggers 2 Process cycles per second.
  - Thermal Impact: Contributes continuous heat generation. If the player goes
    AFK without adequate cooling, miner_d.exe will overheat the system and cause
    a BSOD.

2. Auto-Flush Alpha (flush_d.exe)

  - Unlocked: Level 20
  - RAM Allocation Overhead: Consumes 32 MB of RAM.
  - Behavior: Monitored rule-set. Automatically triggers a Flush when:
    \text{ramUsed} \ge 0.90 \times \text{ramMax} \quad \text{OR} \quad \text{heat} \ge 96.0^\circ\text{C}
  - Balance Limitation: flush_d.exe has a 0.5-second processing delay. If heat
    spikes faster than the cooling system can stabilize during the channel, a
    crash can still occur.

3. Overclock Optimizer (governor_d.exe)

  - Unlocked: Level 40
  - RAM Allocation Overhead: Consumes 128 MB of RAM.
  - Behavior: Dynamically modulates active process speed. It throttles daemon
    activity when heat exceeds 97.0°C and accelerates execution to maximum speed
    when heat drops below 86.0°C to stay within the Thermal Surge window.

